-- title:
--   Zariski-local invariant coordinates for an 𝒪_D-stable subgroup ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $B$ a commutative Noetherian ring in which $p$ is nilpotent. Let $X$ be a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over $B$: a commutative two-dimensional formal group law $X.F$ on $B[\![x_1,x_2]\!]$ together with an action `act` of $\mathbb{Z}_{p^2}=W(\mathbb{F}_{p^2})$ by endomorphisms of the law, a further endomorphism `varpi` with `varpi ∘ varpi` the action of $p$ and `varpi ∘ act a = act (frob a) ∘ varpi`. Let $I\subseteq B[\![x_1,x_2]\!]$ be an ideal and $h\in\mathbb{N}$, subject to: $B[\![x_1,x_2]\!]/I$ is a finite projective $B$-module; for every field $\kappa$ and ring map $f\colon B\to\kappa$ the quotient $\kappa[\![x_1,x_2]\!]/I\kappa[\![x_1,x_2]\!]$ has $\kappa$-dimension $p^h$; some power $q$ satisfies $x_i^q\in I$ for both $i$; every $f\in I$ has zero constant coefficient; for $f\in I$ the series $f(F(x,y))$ lies in the ideal of $B[\![x,y]\!]$ generated by $I(x)\cup I(y)$; and $I$ is stable under substitution of `act a` for every $a$ and of `varpi`. Then there are $n$ and $g\colon \mathrm{Fin}\,n\to B$ generating the unit ideal such that for each $i$, writing $B'=$ `Localization.Away (g i)`, there is a pair $u=(u_1,u_2)$ of power series in $B'[\![x_1,x_2]\!]$ with zero constant coefficients, each invariant in the sense that $u_j(F(x,y))-u_j(x)$ lies in the ideal generated by $I(y)$, with $(u_1,u_2)=I\,B'[\![x_1,x_2]\!]$, and such that every invariant $w\in B'[\![x_1,x_2]\!]$ is $W(u_1,u_2)$ for a unique $W$.
--
--   This is the local structure theorem for the ring of invariants of a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module law under a finite locally free infinitesimal $\mathcal{O}_D$-stable subgroup of degree $p^h$: Zariski-locally on the base that ring is a power-series ring on two invariant coordinates which moreover generate the subgroup ideal. It is the input to the construction of the quotient isogeny, used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_cover_isIsogenyOfHeight_span_range_eq_map_of_subgroup_ideal`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_cover_isIsogenyOfHeight_span_range_eq_map_of_subgroup_ideal).
